{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQUzHPNCaAiPgHgkxPEX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Noted: customers pick 2, 3, or 4 equal installments. Two smaller details follow from that, and I'll use these defaults unless you say otherwise:\n- **Rounding:** when the total doesn't split evenly, the leftover cents go on the last installment. For example, $100 in 3 installments becomes $33.33, $33.33, $33.34.\n- **When they can choose:** only while the invoice is `sent` and nothing has been paid yet.\n\nI still need your call on these, most important first:\n\n1. **Late fees.** If an installment is missed, is the fee 2% of that installment or 2% of the invoice total? Is it charged once per missed installment or once per invoice?\n2. **Overdue status.** Does one missed installment make the whole invoice `overdue`?\n3. **Schedule.** Is the first installment due on the invoice's current due date, with the rest monthly after that?\n4. **Payments.** Does each payment cover the earliest unpaid installment first, with any extra rolling forward?\n5. **Reminders.** Should customers get a reminder 3 days before each installment is due?\n6. **Overdue logic.** Should I build the step that marks invoices overdue and adds the fee? Nothing in the code does that yet.\n\nMy suggestions from before still apply: a 2% fee on each missed installment, charged once per installment; `overdue` while any installment is past due; and yes to 3, 4, 5 and 6. You can just answer \"defaults\" to accept all of those."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":973,"cache_read_input_tokens":31344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":973},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_too